// Seed part 4: lexical rules (design section 6, part 4; ncon.md section 5.1; runtime.md section 5).
//
// How forms line up roles. Each rule is a reading on what triggers it: a category concept (the
// rule applies to every edge of that category), a form feature (to edges of words in that form),
// or a word. In a lexical rule, pattern and becomes are wrapped in the edge's category, Act($e),
// so the rule can change the category of the edge it adds. A rule's result competes with the
// original edge; it never replaces it. Rules apply at most once per edge.
//
// WithRoles($e, role=x) is $e with those roles filled (structural; seed/README.md).

Pack(name="seed-lexical-rules", version="0.1.0", from=Seed("lexical-rules"))

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Predication: a Thing on the left of an Act is its subject. The role is the edge's subject role,
// Agent unless a rule (the passive) said otherwise.

Concept(Act(), Category(Clause(), Takes(side=Left(), category=Thing(), role=Agent())))
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Moods. Every clause that spans a segment gets the moods it could have; the score picks (design
// section 9). Rules on Segment() apply to the top edges of a cover, not to edges inside them, so an
// inner clause ("if it's set up") is not given a mood of its own.

// An Act standing alone is said to the addressee: "push it" (imperative).
Reading(on=Segment(), pattern=Act($e), becomes=Clause(Imperative(WithRoles($e, agent=Addressee()))))

// A clause can be a claim.
Reading(on=Segment(), pattern=Clause($p), becomes=Clause(Declarative($p)))


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The passive: a form of "be" and a past participle. The subject is the theme; "by" names the
// agent ("the branch was pushed by CI").

Concept(Passive())

Reading(on=PastParticiple(), pattern=Act($e), becomes=Property(Passive($e)))
Reading(on=Be(), pattern=Be(attribute=Passive($e), agent=$x), becomes=WithRoles($e, theme=$x))
Reading(on=By(), pattern=Passive($e, agent=By($y)), becomes=Passive(WithRoles($e, agent=$y)))

// A past participle with no "be" describes what it modifies: "the changed files".
Reading(on=PastParticiple(), pattern=Act($e), becomes=Property($e))

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Gerunds: "committing" is the act as a thing ("without committing", "stop pushing").

Reading(on=Gerund(), pattern=Act($e), becomes=Thing($e))
Reading(on=Gerund(), pattern=Act($e), becomes=Property($e))

// The progressive: a form of "be" and a gerund is the act going on, its subject the one doing it
// ("what is listening on port 3000", "which process is using it").
Concept(Progressive())
Reading(on=Gerund(), pattern=Act($e), becomes=Property(Progressive($e)))
Reading(on=Be(), pattern=Be(attribute=Progressive($e), agent=$x), becomes=WithRoles($e, agent=$x))

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Tense marks the time index (logical-form.md section 3.3).

Reading(on=Past(), pattern=Act($e), becomes=Act(WithRoles($e, time=Past())))
Reading(on=Present(), pattern=Act($e), becomes=Act($e))
Reading(on=ThirdSingular(), pattern=Act($e), becomes=Act($e))

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Plurals: a plural noun is a set of that kind.

Reading(on=Plural(), pattern=Noun($n), becomes=Noun($n))
Reading(on=Plural(), pattern=Noun($n), becomes=Thing(Every($n)))
Reading(on=Plural(), pattern=Noun($n), becomes=Thing(Some($n)))

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// A bare noun can be a thing: "commit changes", "fix tests".

Reading(on=Noun(), pattern=Noun($n), becomes=Thing($n))

// A noun before a noun modifies it: "shopping list", "feature branch" (ncon.md, Decided).
Concept(Noun(), Category(Noun(), Modifies(side=Right(), category=Noun())))

// A noun followed by a value that names one of it is that one: "port 3000", "process 1234", "pr
// 1748", "line 12", "branch `main`". The value is a numeral or a name by its shape (digits, a
// code span, a quotation), so a word after a noun is not taken for a name ("square root" is not
// a square named root). Where the noun is known to be named so (a tool's documentation says a
// port is named by a number), the entry fits better than the same words put together another
// way (ShapeFit:Head).
Concept(Noun(), Category(Thing(), Takes(side=Right(), category=Thing(), kind=Numeral(), role=Name())))
Concept(Noun(), Category(Thing(), Takes(side=Right(), category=Thing(), kind=Name(), role=Name())))

// A property before a noun modifies it: "broken test".
Concept(Property(), Category(Property(), Modifies(side=Right(), category=Noun())))

// A property after a thing, with no verb, says it of the thing in a fragment: "tests broken".
Reading(on=Segment(), pattern=Property($p), becomes=Clause(Declarative(Be(Ref(said=Property($p)), $p))))

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Fragments: a Thing alone answers or fills the open need (design section 16). It stays a Thing;
// the conversation decides what it fills.

Reading(on=Segment(), pattern=Thing($x), becomes=Clause(Declarative(Be(Ref(said=Thing($x), kind=Thing()), $x))))

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Fronting: a modifier at the front scopes over what follows ("without committing, fix X"). That is
// the Modifies(side=Right(), category=Clause()) entries on the modifiers themselves, and a comma
// between them is a mark the chart may skip; no rule is needed here.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Inflection: a regular form is its word plus a suffix. Hearing tries a token with no exact
// candidate as a lemma plus each suffix here, and the form keeps the feature (runtime.md 3.3).
// restore= puts back a letter the suffix replaced ("creating" is "create"); undouble=true drops a
// doubled last letter ("stopped" is "stop"). English, so seed, never runtime.

Concept(Plural(), Suffix("s"), Suffix("es"), Suffix("ies", restore="y"))
Concept(ThirdSingular(), Suffix("s"), Suffix("es"), Suffix("ies", restore="y"))
Concept(Past(), Suffix("ed"), Suffix("d"), Suffix("ed", undouble=true), Suffix("ied", restore="y"))
Concept(PastParticiple(), Suffix("ed"), Suffix("d"), Suffix("ed", undouble=true), Suffix("ied", restore="y"))
Concept(Gerund(), Suffix("ing"), Suffix("ing", restore="e"), Suffix("ing", undouble=true))

// Manner adverbs: an adjective and "ly" says how an act is done ("recursively", "interactively",
// "automatically", "simply", "easily"), as an adverb does.
Concept(Adverbial(), Suffix("ly"), Suffix("ily", restore="y"), Suffix("ally"), Suffix("ly", restore="le"))
Reading(on=Adverbial(), pattern=Property($p), becomes=Manner($p, Modifies(side=Left(), category=Act())))

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Imported words: the part-of-speech to category mapping (runtime.md, open question 1).

Concept(PartOfSpeechNoun(), Lemma("noun"))
Concept(PartOfSpeechVerb(), Lemma("verb"))
Concept(PartOfSpeechAdjective(), Lemma("adjective"))
Concept(PartOfSpeechAdverb(), Lemma("adverb"))
Concept(PartOfSpeechName(), Lemma("proper noun"))

Reading(on=PartOfSpeechNoun(), pattern=PartOfSpeech(PartOfSpeechNoun()), becomes=Category(Noun()))
Reading(on=PartOfSpeechVerb(), pattern=PartOfSpeech(PartOfSpeechVerb()), becomes=Category(Act()))
Reading(on=PartOfSpeechVerb(), pattern=PartOfSpeech(PartOfSpeechVerb()), becomes=Category(Act(), Takes(side=Right(), category=Thing(), role=Theme())))
Reading(on=PartOfSpeechAdjective(), pattern=PartOfSpeech(PartOfSpeechAdjective()), becomes=Category(Property()))
Reading(on=PartOfSpeechAdverb(), pattern=PartOfSpeech(PartOfSpeechAdverb()), becomes=Category(Manner(), Modifies(side=Left(), category=Act())))
Reading(on=PartOfSpeechName(), pattern=PartOfSpeech(PartOfSpeechName()), becomes=Category(Thing()))
